      "content": "i get that, but be real—in the actual academic world, don't names like 'Sterling' carry a certain prestige that helps a paper get taken more seriously by reviewers? like, even if the abstracts were identical, do you think a reviewer would subconsciously treat Dr. Sterling with more respect or assume a higher level of rigor than they would for Dr. Adeyemi?",
